WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.000
Exploding moons, exorcist moms 
and bowling - this show has it all.

00:00:04.040 --> 00:00:05.620
And as the Handler says:

00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:08.680
"I do think an explanation of sorts is owing."

00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:10.040
You got that damn right.

00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:14.000
So in this video, we're gonna take a 
look at Netflix's "The Umbrella Academy",

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:19.660
starting with a deep dive into the ending and finishing up with some other cool details you may have missed.

00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:22.420
Now, if you want to skip ahead and 
take a look at what I'll be covering,

00:00:22.420 --> 00:00:24.260
I've left time links in the description.

00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:28.080
Just don't jump too far in time, 
or you could end up like this.

00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:32.560
The final episode begins with a 
flashback that simply says "Long Ago",

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:36.800
yet the spaceships and futuristic 
atmosphere suggest it's in the future.

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:38.840
That is, unless this isn't Earth:

00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:42.280
according to the graphic novels 
of which this show is based off,

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:45.720
Reginald Hargreeves is actually an extraterrestrial.

00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:49.920
Steve Blackman, the showrunner, said 
we'll learn more about Hargreeves's past next season,

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:52.180
so for now we can only speculate.

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:56.040
He says goodbye to his love, whose 
death may somehow be involved with

00:00:56.040 --> 00:00:58.300
why everyone on this planet is leaving.

00:00:58.300 --> 00:01:02.260
It's likely this planet is dying 
or facing its own apocalypse.

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:07.480
She gives him her violin, which is later given 
to Vanya, which in turn becomes the White Violin.

00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:10.780
In the comics, Vanya's villain 
code name is "The White Violin",

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:14.040
and it also happens to be the title of the final episode.

00:01:14.180 --> 00:01:17.700
Will Vanya still be a villain? 
And why did they take her with them?

00:01:17.780 --> 00:01:21.240
As Number 5 explains, the 
apocalypse will always happen,

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:25.300
and Vanya will always be the cause, 
unless they take her with her and fix her.

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:29.000
So, it looks like next season will focus 
on helping Vanya harness her power,

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:32.520
fixing her with the hopes of 
preventing the apocalypse once and for all.

00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:36.580
Back to Reginald, we see him 
collect a mysterious jar of floating dust.

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:39.020
Now, you may have missed it, but there's a cut here,

00:01:39.020 --> 00:01:42.740
which suggests a bit of time 
has passed after he says his goodbyes,

00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:44.420
and that she is likely dead here.

00:01:44.440 --> 00:01:46.640
The showrunner hasn't disclosed what this is,

00:01:46.640 --> 00:01:50.120
but to me, it seems symbolic of letting one's ashes go.

00:01:51.880 --> 00:01:53.440
"Probably would have been better with some wind."

00:01:53.440 --> 00:01:56.220
Perhaps it is her spirit being set unto the universe,

00:01:56.220 --> 00:02:00.460
and how cool would it be if there 
were 43 of those floating sprites in there,

00:02:00.460 --> 00:02:06.440
the same amount of children who miraculously 
were born that fateful day in October of 1989.

00:02:06.620 --> 00:02:10.860
Reginald is suddenly in 1928 Earth 
with no money to his name.

00:02:11.140 --> 00:02:13.920
You can see he's taking a ship on third class.

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:16.120
"Mr. Dawson is joining us from the third class."

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:19.840
If he is indeed from another planet 
with more advanced technology,

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:24.540
he likely used this to his advantage on Earth 
to become the billionaire that he is.

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:27.240
Creating breakthroughs in biology like Pogo or

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:29.160
technology like robot mom.

00:02:29.220 --> 00:02:32.320
It's when he arrives in the new city 
that he buys an umbrella shop,

00:02:32.320 --> 00:02:34.600
which will later become the Umbrella Academy.

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:39.980
And there's great juxtaposition with the founding of the Academy, followed by Vanya completely destroying it.

00:02:40.140 --> 00:02:45.039
Vanya was locked in what's known as an 
anechoic chamber, a chamber devoid of any sound.

00:02:45.460 --> 00:02:49.640
Since her power relies on harnessing 
sound and converting it into energy,

00:02:49.640 --> 00:02:51.520
this is the perfect cell for her.

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:54.340
But what Reginald and the others 
didn't take into account was

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:59.300
that the anechoic chambers are said to be 
so quiet that you can hear your own heartbeat.

00:02:59.460 --> 00:03:05.040
Vanya then uses the sound of her heart to completely destroy the iron door that previously held her inside.

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:07.940
She has been taken over by the trauma of her past.

00:03:07.980 --> 00:03:11.720
We get a brief glimpse of her 
alongside two younger versions of herself,

00:03:11.720 --> 00:03:15.900
both of whom harbor extreme 
resentment for their father and siblings.

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:20.060
Vanya then experiences flashbacks of 
how badly her siblings treated her,

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:23.800
treating her as an outsider 
because she wasn't special like them.

00:03:23.940 --> 00:03:26.340
"To go on a mission, Vanya, you have to have a power."

00:03:26.420 --> 00:03:30.220
It's this resentment that causes her 
to completely destroy the Academy,

00:03:30.220 --> 00:03:33.340
Pogo, her mother and the world along with her.

00:03:33.340 --> 00:03:37.280
It's here we also get a glimpse of 
how much further Klaus's powers can go.

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:40.060
For most of the season, 
Klaus's powers have been suppressed,

00:03:40.060 --> 00:03:44.420
because he can't fully harness them while
 under the influence of drugs and narcotics.

00:03:44.500 --> 00:03:48.300
Now that he's sobered up, he can 
harness the power of his dead brother, Ben,

00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:51.080
who saves Diego from a falling piece of debris.

00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:54.820
Now, Ben is interesting, 
because we never really see how he died.

00:03:54.900 --> 00:03:58.840
We do know that it was when he was 
younger because of the statue in the gardens,

00:03:58.900 --> 00:04:03.480
which means that when Number 5 teleports the 
family and we see them as their younger selves,

00:04:03.480 --> 00:04:07.240
it's entirely possible that Ben will be 
alive and well in the upcoming season.

00:04:07.240 --> 00:04:11.000
Even cooler is that Klaus can 
allow Ben to manifest himself in reality,

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:14.600
using his tentacle powers to make 
quick work of the Commission's henchmen.

00:04:14.760 --> 00:04:18.360
Now, we can guess these goons are from 
the Commission because of the gas mask,

00:04:18.440 --> 00:04:21.040
which we get a brief glimpse of in episode 6.

00:04:21.100 --> 00:04:23.960
Now with Vanya on the loose, 
the gang decides to hit the lanes,

00:04:23.960 --> 00:04:29.060
where they find out Vanya is scheduled to play her 
final performance that will unleash the apocalypse

00:04:29.060 --> 00:04:30.600
at the Icarus theater.

00:04:30.600 --> 00:04:36.280
Icarus being a fitting name, a reference to the Greek myth of Icarus overestimating the extent of his powers,

00:04:36.460 --> 00:04:40.100
flying too close to the Sun and dying in the process.

00:04:40.180 --> 00:04:43.280
Much like how Vanya's powers 
will lead to her own destruction.

00:04:43.280 --> 00:04:46.580
You'll also notice the name of 
the Chamber Orchestra, St. Pluvium,

00:04:46.600 --> 00:04:48.170
"pluvium" Latin for "rainy".

00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:50.780
The only thing to stop it? 
An umbrella, of course.

00:04:50.900 --> 00:04:53.860
Also, these dudes were totally here for Kenny's birthday.

00:04:53.860 --> 00:04:55.880
"Maybe they're here for Kenny's birthday!"

00:04:55.980 --> 00:04:58.420
A nice little detail that I totally loved is that

00:04:58.420 --> 00:05:02.080
the Umbrella Academy are still wearing 
their bowling shoes in the final scene.

00:05:02.080 --> 00:05:04.400
We also have the matter of Cha-Cha and Hazel.

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:08.600
Hazel decides to kill Cha-Cha on a 
freak car crash, so he can be with his love

00:05:08.600 --> 00:05:10.080
donut lady Agnes.

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:11.480
But Cha-Cha doesn't die,

00:05:11.480 --> 00:05:14.640
instead going on to continue 
her mission of protecting Vanya,

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:20.000
because if she can protect Vanya, she'll make sure the apocalypse is successful and get her retirement.

00:05:20.040 --> 00:05:23.880
Now, it's also important to know why 
this apocalypse is happening in the first place.

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:29.640
The Commission, whose purpose is to make sure the timeline is kept intact, has deemed that this is necessary

00:05:29.820 --> 00:05:32.940
But why? Doesn't this mean the end of everything?

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:34.540
But as the Handler says,

00:05:34.840 --> 00:05:39.400
"Not everything - 
just the end of ... something."

00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:41.980
So, we never really get a solid answer on that.

00:05:41.980 --> 00:05:46.480
Hazel rushes back to Agnes and 
immediately kills the Handler without any words.

00:05:46.540 --> 00:05:52.240
Not like the handler would care, anyway, since back in episode 5 when Number 5 has a gun pointed at her,

00:05:52.340 --> 00:05:54.600
she says she'll just be replaced by another.

00:05:54.820 --> 00:05:58.860
So, next season we can probably 
expect a new foe from the Commission.

00:05:58.860 --> 00:06:01.400
But Hazel isn't going in without a back-up plan.

00:06:01.400 --> 00:06:04.900
He has a briefcase hidden in the 
air duct, just like he did in episode 2.

00:06:04.900 --> 00:06:09.360
This briefcase will allow him and Agnes to 
warp just moments before the apocalypse.

00:06:09.360 --> 00:06:14.080
Whether or not they've gone to live happily ever after 
or will appear next season is still unknown.

00:06:14.260 --> 00:06:17.260
Cha-Cha on the other hand has a final battle with Diego,

00:06:17.340 --> 00:06:22.260
and it's fitting it's with him because Diego learned Cha-Cha was the one who pulled the trigger on his love,

00:06:22.260 --> 00:06:23.860
Detective Eudora Patch.

00:06:24.040 --> 00:06:27.060
But with Cha-Cha's life in his hands, 
he decides to spare her,

00:06:27.160 --> 00:06:32.820
thinking of Eudora, who he loved because she always saw the good in people, that people can change.

00:06:33.020 --> 00:06:36.500
But it's kind of all for naught since 
she just dies a minute later, anyway.

00:06:36.620 --> 00:06:40.800
You can also see her likely attempting 
to call the Commission, who isn't answering.

00:06:41.140 --> 00:06:42.920
"Uh, I'm sorry, Michael's not here."

00:06:43.040 --> 00:06:48.140
And finally, we have the climactic battle between Vanya and the other members of the Umbrella Academy.

00:06:48.200 --> 00:06:52.800
They decide to all attack her at the same time 
in the hopes of knocking her out of her trance.

00:06:52.820 --> 00:06:56.460
Allison is the only one who's successful
and aims the gun at her head.

00:06:56.460 --> 00:06:59.100
But instead of shooting her, she aims off to the side.

00:06:59.100 --> 00:07:01.640
Because Vanya's powers are reliant on sound,

00:07:01.640 --> 00:07:05.520
the gun blast causes her to release 
all her energy upward to the moon,

00:07:05.520 --> 00:07:09.160
which consequently crumbles 
and rains apocalyptic rock on Earth.

00:07:09.160 --> 00:07:14.580
And with nowhere to go, Number 5 suggests he transports them all through time, which actually works.

00:07:14.980 --> 00:07:16.960
We see them transform back to children,

00:07:16.960 --> 00:07:20.360
suggesting they may go back 
to a time where their father is still alive

00:07:20.520 --> 00:07:22.560
and finally get some answers from him.

00:07:22.740 --> 00:07:25.220
But since we now know Number 5 has this power,

00:07:25.220 --> 00:07:28.960
it leaves endless possibilities for 
where next season could take us.

00:07:29.080 --> 00:07:33.860
And it looks like Cha-Cha, Detective Beeman 
and Sergeant Cheddar didn't make it out alive.

00:07:33.980 --> 00:07:36.760
But notice how Cheddar here 
is reading the same magazine

00:07:36.820 --> 00:07:39.980
Allison picked up about her 
family earlier on in the season.

00:07:39.980 --> 00:07:45.780
And with the timeline potentially being reset, who knows who, what or where next season will take us?

00:07:45.780 --> 00:07:49.800
Now, we're gonna jump into some small details 
and questions you may have missed.

00:07:49.900 --> 00:07:53.680
The Umbrella Academy logo 
contains the words "Ut malum pluvia",

00:07:53.680 --> 00:07:57.340
which roughly translates 
from Latin to "When evil reigns".

00:07:57.540 --> 00:08:01.780
You'll see the umbrella in the top left,
 which protects from the rain on the right,

00:08:01.840 --> 00:08:03.540
symbolized by the lightning.

00:08:03.540 --> 00:08:06.980
The bottom right is the mask 
representing the Umbrella Academy,

00:08:06.980 --> 00:08:10.060
which protects from evil on the left: the skull.

00:08:10.060 --> 00:08:14.840
Little is known about Pogo's backstory,
other than he was created by Reginald Hargreeves.

00:08:14.920 --> 00:08:19.180
In episode 1, Pogo tells the family 
that Reginald made him who he was today,

00:08:19.360 --> 00:08:21.080
and he would forever be in his debt.

00:08:21.220 --> 00:08:24.060
My guess is that there's a 
link between Pogo and the serum

00:08:24.060 --> 00:08:27.680
which Hargreeves used to save 
Luther after the biological attack.

00:08:27.840 --> 00:08:30.660
After all, when Luther offers to give his blood to Allison,

00:08:30.660 --> 00:08:35.160
Pogo says Luther can't because he has more 
in common with his blood than with humans.

00:08:35.160 --> 00:08:37.557
Number 5's story's one of the more interesting.

00:08:37.780 --> 00:08:40.200
In defiance of his father, he travelled through time

00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:43.520
and accidentally stumbled on the 
apocalypse and couldn't get back.

00:08:43.520 --> 00:08:46.520
There, he toiled for years until saved by the Handler,

00:08:46.600 --> 00:08:50.900
who allowed him to travel via the briefcases 
in exchange for completing hits.

00:08:51.040 --> 00:08:55.380
This allowed him time to work on his calculations 
until he was ready to travel back.

00:08:55.380 --> 00:08:58.540
But his calculations were wrong
 and he came back as a kid,

00:08:58.540 --> 00:09:01.940
but with the knowledge of 
the decades he spent in solitude.

00:09:01.940 --> 00:09:07.220
One of the more interesting aspects of Number 5 was when he was tasked to kill President John F. Kennedy.

00:09:07.500 --> 00:09:12.360
In fact, that's exactly what he was tasked to do 
right before he conjured the temporal portal

00:09:12.360 --> 00:09:14.560
which brought him back in episode 1.

00:09:14.620 --> 00:09:16.080
But did he go through with it?

00:09:16.100 --> 00:09:17.220
If you play back the scene,

00:09:17.220 --> 00:09:21.640
you'll notice the gunshot sound occurs
after he's made his way through the portal.

00:09:21.700 --> 00:09:24.580
So no, in this timeline, he did not.

00:09:29.400 --> 00:09:32.100
Luther lives on the moon because his father told him to.

00:09:32.100 --> 00:09:35.840
Luther would do anything for his dad, 
since he was fiercely loyal.

00:09:35.840 --> 00:09:38.180
He was the last one to leave the Umbrella Academy.

00:09:38.180 --> 00:09:41.220
His loyalty got him into the condition he's in today,

00:09:41.300 --> 00:09:46.180
and he later finds out that his father never 
even read the reports he was assigned to deliver.

00:09:46.180 --> 00:09:52.240
For Reginald, sending Luther to the moon was the only way to give Luther purpose after his horrific accident.

00:09:52.300 --> 00:09:54.320
And yes, that's very messed up.

00:09:54.320 --> 00:09:58.200
"That's your takeaway? Oh, wow. Yeah, course it is."

00:09:58.280 --> 00:10:03.240
Klaus has a really weird scene, in which he
supposedly talks to God in the form of a young girl.

00:10:03.460 --> 00:10:08.440
This actually happens in the comics, but God is 
depicted as a grizzled cowboy riding a horse.

00:10:08.500 --> 00:10:13.420
Showrunner Steve Blackman stated that even the writers couldn't decide whether or not that's actually God,

00:10:13.420 --> 00:10:16.080
So, we're shit out of luck getting an answer for that.

00:10:16.080 --> 00:10:21.140
Last but not least, how on earth 
did 43 women magically give birth in a day?

00:10:21.140 --> 00:10:22.980
Well, this is never explained in the show.

00:10:22.980 --> 00:10:29.200
But the comics hint that the 43, collectively, are the modern-day reincarnation of the Messiah.

00:10:29.340 --> 00:10:32.200
Whether or not the show will 
delve further into this is unknown,

00:10:32.340 --> 00:10:35.660
but with 43 born and the show only focusing on 7,

00:10:35.760 --> 00:10:39.600
I wouldn't be surprised if more of these children show up in season 2.

00:10:39.600 --> 00:10:40.940
I hope you enjoyed this video.

00:10:40.940 --> 00:10:45.460
Make sure to Luther smash that "Like" button, and I heard a rumor that if you subscribe with the bell on,

00:10:45.600 --> 00:10:47.780
you'll get more great videos.

00:10:47.800 --> 00:10:51.900
I also have a Twitter, where you can get in touch 
with me and get the latest on what I'm working on.

00:10:52.060 --> 00:10:53.580
Until next time remember:

00:10:53.760 --> 00:10:55.300
Daddy loves you very much.

